1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,520
What happened at Pompeii?

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,240
Explained like you are 5.

3
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:04,240
Step 1.

4
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:05,640
It is 79 AD.

5
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:08,400
Pompeii is a Roman city of 20,000 people.

6
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,880
Wealthy, busy, full of markets, bathhouses, and taverns, the city sits at the base of

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,640
a large mountain, Mount Vesuvius.

8
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,520
Nobody knows it is a volcano.

9
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,600
The Romans have no word for volcano.

10
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,040
No eruption has been recorded in living memory.

11
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:26,960
The mountain is simply there, beautiful, covered in vineyards, the soil around it, the richest

12
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:27,960
in the region.

13
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:30,800
Because of what is inside it, nobody knows that either.

14
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,800
Step 2.

15
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,720
In February of 79 AD, the ground starts shaking.

16
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:37,640
Wells dry up overnight.

17
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,340
Animals refuse to enter the city.

18
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,680
The Romans interpret these as bad omens.

19
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:43,920
They sacrifice animals to the gods.

20
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,400
They do not evacuate.

21
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:50,800
On the 24th of August 79 AD at 1 PM, Vesuvius explodes.

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,400
A column of ash and gas shoots 21 miles into the sky.

23
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:58,520
It is 100,000 times more powerful than the Hiroshima bomb.

24
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,400
The sky turns black at noon.

25
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,360
Ash begins falling like snow.

26
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,560
Step 3.

27
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,220
Most people try to wait it out indoors.

28
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,580
This is the wrong decision.

29
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,280
The ash builds on rooftops.

30
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,080
Buildings collapse under the weight.

31
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,640
Then the pyroclastic surge.

32
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:17,120
A wave of superheated gas and ash moving at 180 mph, 700 degrees.

33
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,040
It reaches Pompeii in four minutes.

34
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:21,160
Everyone still in the city dies instantly.

35
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,160
Not slowly.

36
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,160
Instantly.

37
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,560
So extreme it vaporizes flesh.

38
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,560
What remains?

39
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:29,000
Body-shaped voids in the hardened ash.

40
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Step 4.

41
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,740
Pompeii is buried under 20 feet of volcanic material and forgotten.

42
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:40,640
For 1,700 years, rediscovered in 1748, excavations find the city exactly as it was left.

43
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,920
Bread still in the ovens.

44
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,120
Graffiti still on the walls.

45
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,880
The body voids filled with plaster reveal people in their final positions.

46
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,120
A dog.

47
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,640
A family huddled together.

48
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,200
A man covering his face.

49
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,160
The most complete snapshot of ancient Roman life ever found.

50
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,880
Preserved perfectly by the thing that destroyed it.

51
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:01,080
And that's just one story inside paladin.

52
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:06,120
It's like Duolingo, but for history lovers, download it now and become the most intelligent

53
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,080
person in the room.

